Subject: [PATCH 38/60] =?UTF-8?q?fix(test):=20make=20deacon=20idle-guard?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20fake=20tmux=20hermetic=20=E2=80=94=20no=20180s=20WaitForComm?=
 =?UTF-8?q?and=20hang=20(gfork-g0d)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TestCheckDeaconHeartbeat_IdleGuard's "very stale" subtest drives the escalation
path: checkDeaconHeartbeat -> restartStuckDeacon -> ensureDeaconRunning ->
deacon.Manager.Start -> tmux.WaitForCommand. WaitForCommand polls display-message
for the pane's foreground command until it is no longer a shell (Claude started)
or ClaudeStartTimeout (180s) elapses. The fake tmux returned empty output for
#{pane_current_command}, so GetPaneCommand errored every poll and the loop ran the
full 180s, timing out the whole daemon package under `go test -race`.

Teach the fake tmux to answer the two display-message queries WaitForCommand/
isPaneDead issue: #{pane_current_command} -> "claude" (a non-shell command, so
WaitForCommand returns on the first poll) and #{pane_dead} -> "0". The very-stale
subtest now completes in ~2.3s (the 2s restart sleep) instead of hanging 180s;
all 5 subtests pass under -race with no race findings.

This is a fork patch on an upstream test file (deacon_idle_guard_test.go is in
base, untouched by any other fork patch) — fork-tax that keeps the mandated
`go test -race ./internal/daemon/...` loop usable on hammer. Scope-verified: only
this one test hung; every boot/crashloop spawn test already passed. Separately,
the package carries one inherited-upstream failure (TestHasAssignedOpenWork...,
fails on pure base 81233d36) tracked as gfork-1bw — out of scope here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 internal/daemon/deacon_idle_guard_test.go | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/internal/daemon/deacon_idle_guard_test.go b/internal/daemon/deacon_idle_guard_test.go
index 81f482cd..f92596a6 100644
--- a/internal/daemon/deacon_idle_guard_test.go
+++ b/internal/daemon/deacon_idle_guard_test.go
@@ -53,6 +53,20 @@ if [[ "$cmd" == "has-session" ]]; then
   exit 0
 fi
 
+# The very-stale escalation subtest drives restartStuckDeacon ->
+# ensureDeaconRunning -> deacon.Manager.Start -> WaitForCommand, which polls
+# display-message for the pane's foreground command until it is no longer a
+# shell (Claude started) or ClaudeStartTimeout (180s) elapses. Report a live
+# pane already running a non-shell command so WaitForCommand returns on the
+# first poll instead of hanging for the full timeout (gfork-g0d).
+if [[ "$cmd" == "display-message" ]]; then
+  case "$*" in
+    *pane_current_command*) echo "claude" ;;
+    *pane_dead*)            echo "0" ;;
+  esac
+  exit 0
+fi
+
 exit 0
 `
 	path := filepath.Join(dir, "tmux")
